    text:"Insurers analyzing hospital billing patterns found that AI-enabled medical coding tools added $942 million to healthcare spending over two years, with a sharp increase in complex-condition documentation that lacks corresponding changes in actual care delivered. A PwC study projects healthcare costs will rise 9% in 2027, the highest increase in 17 years, with nearly 70% of health plans identifying AI-enabled billing as a top cost driver.",
